\par \par  UG-79   Forming shell sections and heads
\par Heat treatment requirements after cold forming\par 
\par Final center line radius             R{\sub f\tab }=
\par Plate thickness                      t\tab =
\par % extreme fiber elongation       75t/R{\sub f\tab }=
\par % extreme fiber elongation       50t/R{\sub f\tab }=
_\par According to UHT-79(a)(1) this piece & be heat treated after cold forming
\par According to UCS-79(d) this piece needs not to be treated after cold forming
\par According to UCS-79(d)(3) this piece shall be treated after cold forming
\par According to UCS-79(d) this piece shall be treated after cold forming
\par if the vessel is in lethal service, or the material shall be impact tested,
\par or the thickness reduction during forming exceeds 10%, or the temperature
\par during forming is in the range of 121°C to 482°C.
